car tester michelle austyn mother says  opel touts the comfort and versatility  of its new Saphira so let's take a look  the compact MPV is well known for its  generous seating a revamp designed now  seeks to further boost its appeal  visually the new Saphira draws on the  design of its little brother the Astra  the infotainment system is also new it  includes apple carplay and android auto  compatibility as well as the Opel OnStar  service assistant since its introduction  in 1999 the Saphira has been known for  its flex 7 seating system which offers  room for up to seven passengers drivers  and passengers who travel long distances  will also appreciate the optional AGR  economic seats which make for a  comfortable and relaxing journey  Michelle says the Saphira also has  excellent handling its panoramic  windshield offers an excellent view of  the road ahead the windshield stretches  from the hood almost to the b-pillar  the version we're testing here has 147  kilowatts of power under the hood and  makes the sprint to 100 km/h and just  under nine seconds Opel Peg's fuel  consumption at 7.2 liters per 100  kilometers  the facelift is most apparent at the  front end with a sporty grille and  chiseled lines the new Saphira boasts a  more dynamic appearance and for the  first time in this category Opel is also  offering the new generation LED  headlights as an add-on but it's in the  rear where the Saphira is still a  standout minimum cargo volume is 710  liters which can be more than doubled  when the second row of seats are folded  the new interior gives a more  uncluttered impression and offers good  connectivity the Opel OnStar service  assistant turns the car into a mobile  Wi-Fi hotspot  here in the second row Michelle says  sliding back the seat is simple the seat  also shifts slightly to the center of  the vehicle for extra roominess creating  a comfortable passenger lounge the new  Saphira offers a choice of engines  including a CNG version the base model  sells for a bit over 21,000 euros in  Germany  ashell sums it up the Opel Zafira offers  good handling and the interior space is  very versatile  so the Saphira is a good family car  that's both spacious and compact enough  for day-to-day driving  in Germany the new Saphira will go on  sale in September  you
 

